<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70230" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεο-δᾱμώδης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ες</span>, a
		Spartan word, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lately made one
				of the people</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δᾶμος</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῆμος</span>
			), <i>newly enfranchised,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δύναται δὲ τὸ ν. ἐλεύθερον ἤδη
					εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.58
				</span></i>
			: applied to Helots freed by the state in reward for service
			in war, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εἵλωσι καὶ ν. καὶ τοῖς περιοίκοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					3.3.6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				5.2.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Myro
			</span></i> I <i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
